# Line endings are part of the acceptance criteria here: the fixture pair
# tests/wrd_v1_0_0.lua -> tests/wrd_v1_0_0_clean.lua is compared byte for byte, and
# the obfuscator's string pool holds the payload's exact bytes.  A checkout that
# rewrites newlines (git's core.autocrlf is true on the Windows runners) would make
# the comparison fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the pipeline, so
# every text file is checked out with LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except the files whose bytes really are binary.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.gz binary
